in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @nl
in @mirror/data

# @mirror/data/toml — TOML as a data-grammar lens.
#
# Parallel species under @mirror/data. Forward-promised stub per
# [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]: declares the family placement,
# the carrier shape, and the parse/emit signatures; bodies land
# when the consumer pulls (the most likely puller is the
# pretty-printer LRM cascade T19 over Cargo.toml / pyproject.toml
# / spec.toml inputs).
#
# === The carrier ===
#
# TOML 1.0.0 (Preston-Werner 2021). The carrier is structurally
# similar to json plus four additional scalar kinds for TOML's
# typed date/time support (per TOML 1.0 §Local Date-Time):
#
#   - offset_datetime  RFC 3339 datetime with timezone offset.
#   - local_datetime   RFC 3339 datetime with no offset.
#   - local_date       Date (no time, no offset).
#   - local_time       Time of day (no date, no offset).
#
# Carrier representations are `text` for now (the wire form is
# canonical; richer typed-time carriers can land when a consumer
# pulls explicit chrono operations — `@mirror/data/toml/datetime`
# sub-species). TOML's integer / float split (`i64` and `f64`
# separately, per the spec) collapses to `number(f64)` for the
# core carrier matching JSON's discipline; an `int` sub-variant
# lands when a consumer pulls integer-precision preservation.
#
# Tables and arrays-of-tables (TOML's defining surface feature)
# parse to `object` and `array(object)` at the carrier level; the
# wire-syntax distinction (`[table]` vs `[[array.of.table]]`) is
# emit-time choice, not carrier-level structure. Inline tables
# (`{key = value}`) parse to the same `object` carrier.
#
# === Lens reading ===
#
# parse(text) -> toml is the focus projection (TOML wire bytes →
# typed structure); emit(toml) -> text is the settle projection.
# The settle projection is where TOML's flavor — table headers,
# dotted-key sugar, multiline-string heredoc — emerges from a
# structurally-flat carrier; the Wadler/Bernardy combinators at
# T17 are well-suited to the table-layout layer (TOML's emit
# choice space is richer than JSON's).
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   toml           Preston-Werner (2013); TOML 1.0 (2021). The
#                  carrier below is TOML 1.0 §Value Types, with
#                  the f64/integer collapse documented above.
#   typed config   Originating in INI files (1985, Microsoft
#                  Windows 3.x); TOML extends INI with explicit
#                  type discipline.
#   datetime as    RFC 3339 (2002, Newman/Klyne); TOML's date/time
#   value          types are the RFC 3339 surface.
#
# Spec context: TOML 1.0 spec (the carrier this species realises),
#               docs/research/2026-06-07-pretty-printer-LRM.md
#               (the cascade T19 expected to pull toml emit for
#               settled Cargo.toml output).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]].
# Substrate recognitions: [[feedback-substrate-pull]],
#                      [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]
#                      (bodies forward-promised).
# Related shards: data.mirror (the family root above),
#                 data/json.mirror (the canonical sibling species),
#                 data/yaml.mirror (sibling — structured-data peer),
#                 data/text.mirror (sibling — the trivial lens).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/mirror/data/toml.mirror`
# declares `@mirror/data/toml` and only that.

prism @mirror/data/toml {
  focus toml
  project toml
  split toml
  shift toml
  settle toml
}

# === The toml carrier ===
#
# TOML 1.0 value types. Core six kinds match json's carrier shape;
# four additional datetime kinds carry RFC 3339 surface forms as
# text. Tables emit through the `object` carrier; emit-time
# chooses inline vs table-header syntax.
type toml = null | bool(bool) | number(f64) | string(text) | array([toml]) | object([(text, toml)]) | offset_datetime(text) | local_datetime(text) | local_date(text) | local_time(text)

# === parse — bytes → toml ===
parse(text) -> toml { \ }

# === emit — toml → bytes ===
emit(toml) -> text { \ }

out @mirror/data/toml
out toml
out parse
out emit
